---
title: Experience
layout: home
description: Where you have worked, what you did there, and what came of it — on a timeline, because a career has an order and a list of jobs does not show it.
eyebrow: Collections
source: src/components/commerce.css · timeline.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap" data-sidebar="on">
	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 2.25rem">
		<header class="im-collhead">
			<p class="im-eyebrow">Experience</p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">Seven years, three places</h1>
			<p class="im-collhead-text">Front-end, then Salesforce, then design systems on my own. Each one taught me the thing the next one needed, which is a sentence you can only write afterwards.</p>
			<p class="im-collhead-meta"><span>2019 — now</span><span>Budapest · remote</span><a href="#roles">Download CV</a></p>
		</header>

		<ol class="im-timeline im-timeline-role im-log" id="roles" style="--im-timeline-gap: 2.5rem">
			{{#each demo.experience}}
			<li class="im-timeline-item" data-state="{{state}}">
				<span class="im-timeline-marker"><span class="im-role-mark">{{mark}}</span></span>
				<time class="im-timeline-time">{{when}}</time>
				<h2 class="im-timeline-title">{{role}}</h2>
				<p class="im-role-at"><b>{{at}}</b></p>
				<ul class="im-role-list">
					{{#each bullets}}<li><span>{{this}}</span></li>{{/each}}
				</ul>
			</li>
			{{/each}}
		</ol>

		<section class="im-section" style="--im-section-gap: 1rem">
			<h2 class="im-caption" data-index="edu">Before that</h2>
			<ol class="im-timeline im-timeline-compact">
				<li class="im-timeline-item" data-state="done"><span class="im-timeline-marker"></span><h3 class="im-timeline-title">BSc Computer Science</h3><time class="im-timeline-time">2015 — 2019</time></li>
				<li class="im-timeline-item" data-state="done"><span class="im-timeline-marker"></span><h3 class="im-timeline-title">Salesforce Platform Developer I</h3><time class="im-timeline-time">2021</time></li>
			</ol>
		</section>
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
			<div class="im-widgets">
				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="x-now">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="x-now">Available</h2>
					<p class="im-widget-heading">Open to design-system work.</p>
					<p>One project at a time, remote, from Budapest.</p>
					<a class="im-btn im-btn-primary im-btn-sm im-btn-block" href="#roles">{{icon "mail"}}Get in touch</a>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="x-skills">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="x-skills">What I do</h2>
					<div class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .375rem">
						<span class="im-tag">Design systems</span>
						<span class="im-tag">CSS</span>
						<span class="im-tag">Tailwind</span>
						<span class="im-tag">Ghost</span>
						<span class="im-tag">Handlebars</span>
						<span class="im-tag">Salesforce</span>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="x-links">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="x-links">Elsewhere</h2>
					<div class="im-widget-products">
						<a class="im-widget-product" href="/collections/project/"><span class="im-widget-product-mark">{{icon "folder"}}</span><span class="im-widget-product-name">Projects</span><span class="im-widget-product-note">6 repositories</span>{{icon "arrow-up-right"}}</a>
						<a class="im-widget-product" href="#roles"><span class="im-widget-product-mark">{{icon "brand-linkedin"}}</span><span class="im-widget-product-name">LinkedIn</span><span class="im-widget-product-note">The formal version</span>{{icon "arrow-up-right"}}</a>
						<a class="im-widget-product" href="#roles"><span class="im-widget-product-mark">{{icon "download"}}</span><span class="im-widget-product-name">CV</span><span class="im-widget-product-note">PDF, one page</span>{{icon "arrow-up-right"}}</a>
					</div>
				</section>
			</div>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>A career has an order</h2>
		<p>Which is why it is a <a href="/components/timeline/">timeline</a> and not a list of cards. The line is the point: it shows that one thing led to the next, and where the gaps are, and how long each of them lasted — none of which a stack of boxes shows.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>im-timeline-role</code></td><td>Tunes the timeline's marker into a square that holds a logo or two letters — so a CV reads as a row of <em>places</em> rather than a row of dots.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-role-mark</code></td><td>What goes in it: an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> if there is a logo, initials if there is not.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-role-at</code></td><td>The employer, under the role. The role is the heading because the role is what a reader is scanning for.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-role-list</code></td><td>What you did. Small drawn bullets, capped at a readable measure.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>data-state</code></td><td><code>current</code> puts the accent ring on the job you are in; <code>done</code> fills the line above it.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>

		<h2>Rules</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Outcomes, not duties.</strong> "Took a nine-minute process to ninety seconds" beats "responsible for process improvement", and it is the only line anybody will remember.</li>
			<li><strong>Three bullets each, at most.</strong> A page with thirty bullets on it has none.</li>
			<li><strong>Do not hide the gaps.</strong> The timeline shows them anyway; a date that quietly overlaps is worse than a year off with a sentence about it.</li>
			<li><strong>Put "available" at the top of the rail.</strong> It is the one thing a visitor to this page might act on.</li>
			<li><strong>Education goes last and small.</strong> After the first job it is context, not evidence.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
